Currently, no. I was in two minds about whether or not the babies
should get the special effects. But I think you're probably right
about them being a bit wimpy, I guess I'll give them the effects. I
don't think it will make much difference anyway.

Incidentally, the special bites aren't actually bonus damage - just a
different damage type. In vanilla nethack, having negative AC reduces
the damage you take from any kind of attack (in addition to making
attacks less likely to hit), but in this mod, damage from elemental
attacks are not reduced by AC - they are only reduced by their
corresponding resistance. For example, if you have  -20 AC, and a
dragon bites for 14 physical damage, on average you'll take 4 damage
(because the damage is reduced by rnd(20). But if it's 14 fire damage,
then you'd take 14 damage if you have no resistance, 7 damage if you
have only intrinsic resistance (50% reduction), and 0 damage if you
have complete resistance (ie. extrinsic resistance). So whether or not
the damage is increased by this change depends on what armour you have
and what resistances you have. --  But regardless of the damage, the
dragons will certainly be more dangerous because of the potential
destruction of items from the elemental dragons, and stun / paralysis
etc from the other dragons.


